## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CV system design under fintech constraints: latency, privacy, and robustness to occlusion and demographic variation.

## Key Concepts
- Monocular 3D face modeling and pose estimation
- On-device adaptation with few-shot learning
- Liveness detection under occlusion
- Synthetic+real data strategies, loss design, and evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: brief outline of 3DMM fitting loop (high level)
function fit3DMM(frame, model) {
  const landmarks = detectLandmarks(frame);
  const pose = solvePnP(landmarks, model.meanShape);
  return {pose, coefficients: model.coeffs};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design a privacy-preserving data pipeline for raw frames on-device?  
- Which metrics would you monitor in production to catch model drift or spoofing attempts?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses on-device CV design, latency budgeting, and robust 3D human pose estimation for safety-critical driving.

## Key Concepts
- On-device real-time inference with a lightweight backbone
- 2D-to-3D pose reconstruction and Kalman filtering
- Self-supervised pretraining from unlabeled video
- Robustness to occlusion and adverse weather
- Quantization and latency accounting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for pipeline
class PedestrianPoseEstimator {
  constructor() { /* load detector, 3D head, PnP module, tracker */ }
  forward(frame) {
    const keypoints2D = this.detector.detect(frame)
    const pose3D = this.poseHead.estimate(keypoints2D)
    const pose6DoF = differentiablePnP(pose3D, this.cameraIntrinsics)
    return this.tracker.update(pose6DoF)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-pedestrian tracking with identity preservation?
- What failure modes are most critical in heavy rain and how would you mitigate them?
